<h2 id="the-problem">The Problem</h2>

<h3 id="how-do-you-read-a-text-file-determine-the-usage-frequency-of-all-words-sort-them-from-high-to-low-and-print-out-a-ranked-list-of-all-words-and-their-frequencies">How do you read a text file, determine the usage frequency of all words, sort them from high to low, and print out a ranked list of all words and their frequencies?</h3>

<blockquote>
  <p>This question comes from a famous event in the history of computer science. It was a challenge posed by Jon Bentley, author of the “Programming Pearls” column in Communications of the ACM magazine, to computer science pioneer Donald Knuth.</p>
